// Deliberately broken, for error-path tests.
//
// Only *recoverable* faults live here. The tokenizer's fatal faults — leading whitespace
// that mixes tabs and spaces, an unclosed "(", an unterminated template — abort the whole
// scan before the parser ever runs, so they are exercised as inline snippets in
// dsl/tests/tokenizer.test.js instead. Everything below should produce one error each,
// with the surrounding statements still parsing cleanly.
using *
    // ERROR: `is` is non-associative, so this chain must be rejected outright.
    await .a is .b is .c
        POST `never reached`
    // ERROR: the pipe operator has no right-hand operand.
    await 1st <|
        POST `never reached`
    // ERROR: `if` opens a block but nothing is indented beneath it.
    if .sender is "nobody"
    // This statement is a sibling of the `if`, not its body, and must still parse.
    POST `still standing`
